      "observed": "C3 is a 100 nF capacitor connected between VCC and the P-MOSFET gate net Net-(Q1-G). The gate net has no resistor to VCC/source; apart from C3 it is only connected to Q1 gate and Q2 collector.",
      "expected": "For a high-side P-MOSFET switched by an NPN driver, the gate needs a DC pull-up to source/VCC (typically a resistor, e.g. 10 kΩ) so that when Q2 turns off the gate returns to source voltage and Q1 turns off. A capacitor alone cannot provide this bias.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C3\") (value \"100nF\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"7\") (name \"Net-(Q1-G)\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C3\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"15\") (name \"VCC\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C3\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C3 VCC Net-_Q1-G_ 100n"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "After Q2 pulls the P-MOSFET gate low, C3 can hold the gate low when Q2 turns off, leaving Q1 on or making the fan PWM switching undefined. The fan may stay on or fail to respond correctly to control.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show a likely anomaly at C3: a capacitor is used as the only gate-bias element on the high-side P-MOSFET, where a pull-up resistor to VCC/source is required for reliable turn-off."
}

